**EXERCISE 2.17.** Establish in detail that the mapping $g : \mathbb{B} \to \mathbb{B}$ of Exercise 2.4 is approximable. Is it uniquely determined by these equations:

$$g(0x) = 0g(x),$$
$$g(11x) = g(1x),$$
$$g(10x) = 0x,$$
$$g(1) = \bot$$

or are some missing?

<!-- page 35 -->

<!-- formalization -->

**Theorem (`exercise_2_17`).** The erase-ones map is the unique approximable endomap of the binary-tree system satisfying the run equations, and those equations hold of the erase-ones map.

*Proof.* Uniqueness among solutions of the run equations, and verification that the erase-ones map satisfies them. Approximability is the construction of the erase-ones map. ∎
